\f1\fs22 She called Hayley. \'93Where are you?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93I\'92m in the control room, monitoring activity,\'94 Hayley answered. \'93Are you okay?\'94\
\'93When are you coming to bed?\'94\
Hayley hesitated. \'93I really need to keep a lid on things here.\'94\
\'93Everyone\'92s gone,\'94 Kathy said with some effort.\
\'93Everyone? What do you mean, everyone?\'94\
\'93Sarah, Chip, Alexander\'85\'94\
Only one name mattered to Hayley. \'93Sarah\'92s gone?\'94\
\'93She said something is going on in the Ironing Room.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In the control room, Hayley looked for a camera feed from the Ironing Room. She was sure Eloise would have it surveilled. When she found the feed, she dragged it to her left-hand monitor and maximised it. Johnny, Chip and Ortolan were there.\
\'93She\'92s not there, yet,\'94 Hayley said as she checked cameras back along the shortest route.\
\'93I\'92m worried about her. She\'92s carrying\'85 a lot,\'94 Kathy said.\
\'93Don\'92t worry, I\'92ll find her.\'94\
Hayley hung up.\
After she\'92d exhausted all the camera angles on the more direct routes between the bunker and the Ironing Room, Hayley became concerned. Where would Sarah go? A toilet? Had Tony called her? Had she gone to meet him at the Traverse? She opened a camera stream on the Ruined Castle concourse, and saw a Jones clone with its pistol aimed at a man with his hands up. The man with the hands was dressed like a politician\'97Hayley felt like she should recognise him. Maybe all successful politicians make you feel like that. The man seemed to be too composed for a politician with an actual gun aimed at him\'97he was PAPER, Hayley guessed, though why a Jones would be threatening him was a mystery.\
Another man came into view, stalking the Jones from behind. Hayley toured the feeds of neighbouring cameras. Hayley enlarged the feed: the stalker held a knife low against his thigh. Worse\'97Hayley realised she recognised this one.\
It was Haloren Smythe.\
Hayley needed to convince herself she had identified him correctly before she called Eloise for a second time in fifteen minutes.
